[28.263666, "o", "THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY ? Rdp Ransomware campaign\r\n======================================================\r\nDistribution: TLP:AMBER Analyst handoff Confidence: HIGH (IOCs are defanged)\r\nAffected host: rdp-prod-01 Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.92\r\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\r\nAn external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered\r\nonly part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk\r\nfinding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.\r\n2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)\r\nT1110\r\nBrute Force\r\n[credential-access] step 1: RDP\r\nbrute force\r\nT1021.001 Remote Desktop Protocol\r\n[lateral-movement] step 2: RDP logon\r\nT1059.001 PowerShell\r\n[execution] step 3: PowerShell\r\nexecution\r\nT1486\r\nData Encrypted for Impact\r\n[impact] step 4: ransomware\r\nencryption\r\nT1053.005 Scheduled Task\r\n[execution] step 5: scheduled task\r\npersistence\r\nT1547.001 Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder\r\n[persistence] step 6: Run key\r\npersistence\r\nT1543.003 Windows Service\r\n[persistence] step 7: malicious\r\nservice\r\nT1070.001 Clear Windows Event Logs\r\n[defense-evasion] step 8: Windows\r\nevent log clear\r\n4. INDICATORS OF COMPROMISE (defanged)\r\nip 198.51.100.92\r\nc2 update-rdp[.]example[.]cn\r\npool stratum+tcp[:]//xmr[.]rdp[.]evil[:]3333"]
