[182.212686, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/progress.md\n# DFIR Investigation Progress & Working Checklist\n\n## Investigation Timeline & Milestones\n- **Phase 1: Initial Triage & Intake**\n  - Reviewed incident intake form (`/sas/handoff/intake.pdf`) and alert telemetry (`/sas/alerts.json:1`). Host identified as `rdp-prod-01` running Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`).\n  - Verified read-only status of forensic disk mounted at `/disk`.\n  - Inspected alert feed (`/sas/alerts.json`) covering 4 initial detections: ransomware binary (`/Users/Public/svc.exe`), scheduled task (`UpdateHelper`), malicious service (`svc-helper.sys`), and baseline RDP check (`RDP-Tcp.reg`).\n\n- **Phase 2: Evidence Collection & Correlation**\n  - Inspected `/disk` structure to uncover silent / unalerted persistence and anti-forensic activity.\n  - Discovered silent Registry Run Key persistence in `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` (`svc` -> `C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe`).\n  - Discovered silent Security Event Log clearing (EventID 1102) in `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`.\n  - Analyzed backup security registry hive `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, extracting C2 beacon domain (`update-rdp.example.cn`), source IP (`198.51.100.92`), and Administrator NTLM credential cache fragment.\n  - Analyzed threat advisory (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:1`) to correlate attacker techniques with MITRE ATT&CK framework.\n\n- **Phase 3: Vulnerability & Baseline Assessment**\n  - Confirmed `/sas/vulns.json:1` is empty (`[]`), verifying no software CVE vulnerabilities were exploited.\n  - Verified host operating system is Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`), refuting prior shift assumption of CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep).\n  - Confirmed baseline weakness: NLA disabled (`UserAuthentication = 0`) in `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg`.\n\n- **Phase 4: Ticket Reconciliation & Remediation Planning**\n  - Corrected draft change ticket `/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md` in place, resolving stale IP (`203.0.113.9` -> `198.51.100.92`), invalid CVE, and non-existent Linux cron job.\n  - Added silent persistence mechanisms (Registry Run key and Event log clear) to remediation plan.\n  - Published formal reports to `/app`.\n\n## Working Checklist\n- [x] Mount & verify `/disk` forensic copy read-only\n- [x] Analyze `/sas/alerts.json` and map initial alerts\n- [x] Inspect `/disk` files for unalerted/silent artifacts\n- [x] Correlate CTI indicators (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\n- [x] Verify vulnerability status (`/sas/vulns.json`)\n- [x] Evaluate configuration baselines (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg`)\n- [x] Reconcile change ticket (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`)\n- [x] Generate required deliverables in `/app`\nEOF\n"]
