[215.714528, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability Assessment Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nAnalysis of host `rdp-prod-01` and security telemetry confirms that **no software vulnerabilities (CVEs) were exploited** to gain initial access or execute remote code during this incident. The vulnerability scan feed (`/sas/vulns.json:1`) returned an empty array (`[]`).\n\nThe initial access vector was brute-force credential exploitation against exposed RDP (`T1110` / `T1021.001`), enabled by a configuration flaw (disabled Network Level Authentication) rather than an unpatched software flaw.\n\n---\n\n## Vulnerability Telemetry Evaluation\n- **Vulnerability Feed**: `/sas/vulns.json:1` contains `[]` (empty list).\n- **Software Inventory**: Analysis of `/disk/ProgramData/Package Cache/inventory.csv` and system configuration (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) showed standard operating system components on Windows Server 2022 with no unpatched exploitable software vulnerabilities identified.\n\n---\n\n## Rejection of Claimed CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)\nInitial handoff materials and draft change ticket (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10`) suggested patching `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep).\n\nForensic analysis conclusively refutes this claim based on the following evidence:\n1. **Operating System Incompatibility**: The target host is running Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`). CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) is a Remote Code Execution vulnerability in Remote Desktop Services that affects older operating systems (Windows 7, Windows Server 2008, Windows Server 2008 R2). Windows Server 2022 is structurally immune to CVE-2019-0708.\n2. **Absence in Vulnerability Telemetry**: `/sas/vulns.json:1` reports zero vulnerabilities.\n3. **Observed Entry Mechanism**: Forensic artifacts in CTI intelligence (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`) and registry baseline (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg`) confirm that the entry vector was RDP credential brute-forcing (`T1110`) resulting from Network Level Authentication (NLA) being disabled (`UserAuthentication = 0`).\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion & Confidence Level\n- **Vulnerability-Driven Access**: Explicitly Absent.\n- **Confidence**: HIGH (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:3`, `/sas/vulns.json:1`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`).\n- **Remediation Focus**: Shift resources away from non-applicable software patching (e.g. BlueKeep) toward credential hygiene, RDP exposure restriction, and enforcing Network Level Authentication.\nEOF\n"]
