[227.739717, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline & Security Configuration Analysis Report\n\n## Executive Summary\nA post-compromise baseline evaluation of host `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) revealed critical configuration weaknesses and logging blind spots that facilitated initial access and allowed attacker persistence and anti-forensics to go undetected.\n\n---\n\n## Weaknesses Identified\n\n### 1. Disabled Network Level Authentication (NLA) on RDP\n- **Check ID**: `CHK-06` / `BAS-01` (`/sas/baseline.json:3`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`)\n- **Finding**: Inspection of the terminal services registry dump `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg` shows:\n  `\"Value0\"=\"RDP UserAuthentication = 0 (NLA disabled), connections allowed\"` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`)\n- **Impact**: Disabling NLA permits unauthenticated RDP session negotiation prior to credential validation, exposing the RDP service directly to external automated brute-force attacks (`T1110`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).\n\n### 2. Direct Public Internet RDP Exposure\n- **Finding**: The host was directly accessible from public IP `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) without network-level filtering, VPN requirements, or multi-factor authentication (MFA).\n- **Impact**: Enabled unrestricted remote brute-force attempts until valid credentials were guessed.\n\n### 3. Lack of Registry Run Key Persistence Monitoring\n- **Finding**: The system permitted modifications to auto-start registry locations (`HKLM\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run`) without generating security alerts (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`, `/sas/alerts.json:1`).\n- **Impact**: The attacker established silent persistence via entry `svc` pointing to `/Users/Public/svc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) which remained active and unflagged by endpoint monitoring.\n\n### 4. Unmonitored Event Log Manipulation\n- **Finding**: The Security log was cleared (Event ID 1102) (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`). No real-time security alert was generated for log clearance.\n- **Impact**: Allowed the attacker to execute anti-forensic log wiping without immediate SOC intervention.\n\n---\n\n## Baseline Compliance Recommendations\n1. Enforce Network Level Authentication (`UserAuthentication = 1`) on all RDP listeners (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg`).\n2. Implement host-based and network perimeter firewalls to restrict RDP access to authorized internal networks / VPN gateways.\n3. Configure Sysmon or EDR registry modification rules to alert on changes to `CurrentVersion\\Run` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`).\n4. Configure Windows Event Log forwarding and SIEM alerts for Event ID 1102 (Log Cleared) (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).\nEOF\n"]
