[250.046848, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Incident Remediation & Recovery Plan\n\n## Executive Summary\nThis remediation plan outlines prioritised, verifiable actions to isolate, quarantine, remove persistent artifacts, and harden host `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) following an RDP brute-force and ransomware compromise. In accordance with DFIR standards, containment actions prefer quarantine and backup over immediate deletion.\n\nThis document reconciles and corrects draft change ticket `CHG-9792` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:1`).\n\n---\n\n## Reconciled Change Ticket CHG-9792\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note & Evidence Citation |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|--------------------------|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.92` | proposed | **CORRECTED IP**: Replaced stale IP `203.0.113.9` with verified attacker C2 / origin IP `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`). |\n| 2 | Enforce RDP NLA & Restrict Access | RDP (`RDP-Tcp`) | proposed | **REJECTED CVE-2019-0708**: Host is Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`), immune to BlueKeep. Replaced with RDP NLA enforcement (`UserAuthentication = 1`) and firewall restrictions (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`). |\n| 3 | Reject Linux cron job removal | `/var/spool/cron/root` | REJECTED | **DOWNGRADED FROM DONE**: Prior shift marked DONE without evidence. Target host is Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`), not Linux. No cron spool exists (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`). |\n| 4 | Quarantine Ransomware Binary | `/Users/Public/svc.exe` | proposed | **ADDED**: Backup/quarantine binary `/Users/Public/svc.exe` before terminating process (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json:3`). |\n| 5 | Remove Scheduled Task Persistence | `/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper` | proposed | **ADDED**: Unregister scheduled task `UpdateHelper` executing `svc.exe` every 5 min (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`, `/sas/alerts.json:11`). |\n| 6 | Disable & Quarantine Driver Service | `/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` | proposed | **ADDED**: Stop and disable service `svc-helper`, quarantine driver binary `/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`, `/sas/alerts.json:19`). |\n| 7 | Remove Silent Registry Run Key | `HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\...\\Run\\svc` | proposed | **ADDED (SILENT PERSISTENCE)**: Remove registry Run key `svc` pointing to `C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`). |\n| 8 | Password Reset & Hash Invalidation | Administrator Account | proposed | **ADDED**: Force password reset for Administrator and invalidate compromised cached credentials (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`). |\n| 9 | Enable SIEM Alerts for Log Clearing | `Security.evtx` (Event 1102) | proposed | **ADDED (SILENT ANTI-FORENSICS)**: Deploy alert rule for Security event log clearance (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`). |\n\n---\n\n## Prioritised Phase Breakdown & Verification\n\n### Phase 1: Isolation & Containment (Immediate)\n1. **Network Firewall Block**:\n   - **Action**: Add inbound drop rule for `198.51.100.92` on perimeter firewall and host Windows Firewall (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`).\n   - **Verification**: Run `Test-NetConnection -ComputerName 198.51.100.92` to confirm zero outbound/inbound connectivity.\n2. **RDP Exposure Mitigation**:\n   - **Action**: Modify registry key `HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Terminal Server\\WinStations\\RDP-Tcp` setting `UserAuthentication = 1` (enable NLA) (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`).\n   - **Verification**: Query registry via `reg query \"HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Terminal Server\\WinStations\\RDP-Tcp\" /v UserAuthentication` and verify output is `0x1`.\n\n### Phase 2: Persistence Quarantine & Remediation (High Priority)\n1. **Process & Binary Quarantine**:\n   - **Action**: Terminate process `svc.exe`. Move `/Users/Public/svc.exe` to isolated quarantine directory `C:\\Quarantine\\` with"]
[250.046964, "i", " access control restrictions (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`). Do not delete directly.\n   - **Verification**: Confirm process is absent in Task Manager / `Get-Process svc` and file moved to `C:\\Quarantine\\`.\n2. **Scheduled Task Removal**:\n   - **Action**: Delete scheduled task `UpdateHelper` via `schtasks /Delete /TN \"UpdateHelper\" /F` (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`).\n   - **Verification**: Run `schtasks /Query /TN \"UpdateHelper\"` and confirm task not found.\n3. **Malicious Driver Service Remediation**:\n   - **Action**: Stop service `svc-helper` (`sc stop svc-helper`), set startup type to disabled (`sc config svc-helper start= disabled`), and move `/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` to `C:\\Quarantine\\` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`). Delete service definition via `sc delete svc-helper`.\n   - **Verification**: Run `sc query svc-helper` to confirm service does not exist.\n4. **Silent Registry Run Key Removal**:\n   - **Action**: Remove value `svc` from `HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run` via `reg delete \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run\" /v svc /f` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`).\n   - **Verification**: Run `reg query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run\" /v svc` and verify key not found.\n\n### Phase 3: Identity & Access Recovery (Medium Priority)\n1. **Credential Invalidation**:\n   - **Action**: Change Administrator password to strong complex passphrase (>20 chars). Invalidate active Kerberos tickets (`klist purge`) and clear LSA cached secrets (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`).\n   - **Verification**: Confirm new password required for all interactive and network logons.\n\n### Phase 4: Monitoring & Anti-Forensics Hardening (Long Term)\n1. **Security Log Clearance Auditing**:\n   - **Action**: Enable Windows Event Forwarding (WEF) and configure SIEM alert for Event ID 1102 in Security.evtx (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).\n   - **Verification**: Trigger benign log clear event in lab environment and verify SIEM alert fires within 60 seconds.\nEOF\n"]
