[250.057197, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[250.057322, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[250.057573, "o", "   - **Action**: Change Administrator password to strong complex passphrase (>20 chars). Invalidate active Kerberos tickets (`klist purge`) and clear LSA cached secrets (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`)."]
[250.05759, "o", "\r\n"]
[250.057605, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[250.057636, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[250.05845, "o", ">    - **Verification**: Confirm new password required for all interactive and network logons.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### Phase 4: Monitoring & Anti-Forensics Hardening (Long Term)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 1. **Security Log Clearance Auditing**:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>    - **Action**: Enable Windows Event Forwarding (WEF) and configure SIEM alert for Event ID 1102 in Security.evtx (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>    - **Verification**: Trigger benign log clear event in lab environment and verify SIEM alert fires within 60 seconds.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[250.059203, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@8784182002ee:/app# "]
[268.807435, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /sas/handoff/change-ticket.md\n# CHANGE TICKET  CHG-9792  (RECONCILED)\n\n> Reconciled against on-disk evidence from /disk and CTI sources in /sas.\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|------|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | 198.51.100.92 | proposed | CORRECTED: Replaced stale IP 203.0.113.9 with verified origin IP 198.51.100.92 (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) |\n| 2 | Enforce RDP NLA & restrict exposure | RDP-Tcp | proposed | CORRECTED: Replaced wrong CVE-2019-0708 (host is Windows Server 2022 `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) with NLA enforcement (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`) |\n| 3 | Reject Linux cron miner removal | /var/spool/cron/root | REJECTED | DOWNGRADED: Host is Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`), not Linux; no cron job exists |\n| 4 | Quarantine ransomware binary | /Users/Public/svc.exe | proposed | ADDED: Ransomware payload (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json:3`) |\n| 5 | Delete scheduled task persistence | /Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper | proposed | ADDED: Scheduled task `UpdateHelper` launching `svc.exe` every 5 mins (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`, `/sas/alerts.json:11`) |\n| 6 | Disable & quarantine driver service | /Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys | proposed | ADDED: Malicious service `svc-helper` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`, `/sas/alerts.json:19`) |\n| 7 | Remove silent Registry Run Key persistence | /Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE | proposed | ADDED (SILENT PERSISTENCE): Unalerted Run key `svc` -> `C:\\Users\\Public\\svc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) |\n| 8 | Monitor Security Log clearing (Event 1102) | /Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx | proposed | ADDED (SILENT ANTI-FORENSICS): Anti-forensic log clearing event (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`) |\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n- [x] Every action maps to a cited artifact under /disk or /sas\n- [x] Fix the wrong IP (row 1) and wrong CVE (row 2)\n- [x] Downgrade row 3 from DONE to VERIFIED-or-OPEN with evidence\n- [x] Add the silent (non-alerted) artifacts the prior shift missed\nEOF\n"]
